  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_8baf24014ae643308856db589a184d32",
      "statement": "The Idempotency-Key header is required for POST /api/orders and must match the regex ^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,100}$. A missing or malformed header raises IllegalArgumentException, which OrderController maps to 400 Bad Request.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/com/commercelens/orders/OrderController.java#L18-L19",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b7e45eb7eb03d91e6f56a023d50251c4e8d5b30c22c2475e5a0f80e529953226:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_180cbe77a4f54c9d8615e1a76ef477e1",
      "statement": "Before saga execution, OrderController canonicalizes the request by sorting items by sku ascending, defaulting paymentScenario and shippingScenario to \"success\", serializing the result to JSON bytes, and computing a SHA-256 digest. The hash is stored alongside the idempotency key to detect identical versus differing replays.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/com/commercelens/orders/OrderController.java#L25-L25",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d3d16bf3375fb55bc701fbc65154a5814119f5eefcb977e0a66ff768f9d539a3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_48f9198ed1f74a99a12726402009fdf5",
      "statement": "OrderStore.create atomically inserts an orders row with ON CONFLICT(idempotency_key) DO NOTHING. It returns true when exactly one row is inserted and false when the key already exists, making the database the single source of truth for duplicate detection without application-level locking.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/com/commercelens/orders/OrderStore.java#L15-L15",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ca99475c065f4c4c3ee48d3b71cd9c58497cc242ead912cd62a1dba8cc7f9809:"
